('CIT_JM_RIKBIEL_ENOCH3','ENT_JM_RIKBIEL','SRC_3_ENOCH','3 Enoch (The Hebrew Book of Enoch)','Enoch 23','Thus the order is the following: (1) The Wheels (Hebrew: Galgallim) of the Merkaba under the prince Rikbiel (from rekeb = chariots). The name Galgallim is derived from Ezek. 10% ® 18, "The Galgallim play the part of the ‘Wheels'' of Ezek. 1 and 10, i.e. they carry the Merkaba. They are at the bottom of the Merkata-structure: "‘the feet of the Hayyop are resting upon them" (19°).','Hugo Odeberg',1928,'https://archive.org/details/ksigaxiienochorthehebrewbookofenoch_202012',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter against a clean edition.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
