('CIT_JM_SERAPHIEL_ENOCH3','ENT_JM_SERAPHIEL','SRC_3_ENOCH','3 Enoch (The Hebrew Book of Enoch)','Enoch 26','(8) Seraphiel H''. See Schwab, VA. p. 260. Among the different passages treating of ‘SERAPHIEL'' that which is nearest akin to the present representation is Zohar, ii. 252 b (Hekaloth), where SERAPHIEL is given as the name of one of the four Seraphim, viz. the first one. Acc. to S. Raziel, 36.b, he is appointed over one of the gates of the heavenly apartments. Acc. to Widduy Yaphe (Add. 15299, fol.','Hugo Odeberg',1928,'https://archive.org/details/ksigaxiienochorthehebrewbookofenoch_202012',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter against a clean edition.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
