('CIT_JM_SOPERIEL_MEHAYYE_ENOCH3','ENT_JM_SOPERIEL_MEHAYYE','SRC_3_ENOCH','3 Enoch (The Hebrew Book of Enoch)','3 Enoch (The Hebrew Book of Enoch)','18: Zakzakiel, 50066 11021, Soferiel Mehayye. Chh. 19 seqq.: Serafim (261). Chh. 30 seqq.: the Prince of the world (30), the Divine Attribute of Mercy (31), the angels of Mercy (33), etc. | The office of Celestial Fudge, whether in general or over the angels only, is in all the rest of the book occupied by the Holy One Himself- although He may be represented as assisted by or taking counsel with certain of the highest angels, e.g.','Hugo Odeberg',1928,'https://archive.org/details/ksigaxiienochorthehebrewbookofenoch_202012',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter against a clean edition.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
