('CIT_JM_ZIQIEL_ENOCH3','ENT_JM_ZIQIEL','SRC_3_ENOCH','3 Enoch (The Hebrew Book of Enoch)','Enoch 14','4: the sun), Sariel (the moon) and Ezeqeel (= Ziqiel of vs. 4: the sparks or lightnings); cf. Zaqiel, Baraqijal (= Baragiel: lightnings), Jomjael (= Yomiel?, prince of the day, here Shimshiel). For the close connection of the gods, angels or rulers of elementary and planetary phenomena attested in Persian religion, Mithraism and Gnosticism cf. Bousset, Hauptprobleme der Gnosis, pp. 223-237. Cf. Diels, Elementum, pp.','Hugo Odeberg',1928,'https://archive.org/details/ksigaxiienochorthehebrewbookofenoch_202012',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter against a clean edition.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_RLMX_SEVEN_HEAVENS_ENOCH3','ENT_RLMX_SEVEN_HEAVENS','SRC_3_ENOCH','3 Enoch (The Hebrew Book of Enoch)','3 Enoch (The Hebrew Book of Enoch)','2 On the various representations of the 70 (or 72) princes of kingdoms, wide notes on 17°, 187°, 307, ORIGIN OF THE CONCEPTION OF METATRON 143 of God''s Absolute Sovereignty over Heavens and Earth, the celestial rulers of necessity became the satraps, viceroys under ‘the King of the Kings of Kings'', appointed as rulers by Him; in this capacity they may fail, or be faithless (a remnant of their character of independent evil agencies) and subsequently be puni','Hugo Odeberg',1928,'https://archive.org/details/ksigaxiienochorthehebrewbookofenoch_202012',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter against a clean edition.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1)
